## 🎯 Key Frameworks Compared

| Framework | Strength | Best For |
|-----------|----------|----------|
| **LangGraph** | Largest ecosystem, stateful orchestration, Python/JS | Production multi-agent workflows |
| **CrewAI** | Role-based collaboration, built-in process management | Team-style agent orchestration |
| **AutoGPT** | Autonomous experimentation | Research, exploration |
| **AutoGen 2.0** | High-concurrency commercial deployments | Enterprise |
| **OpenClaw** | Local-first, privacy-first, system-wide automation | Personal AI assistant, coding automation |
| **PydanticAI** | Type-safe, structured output | Reliability-critical agents |
| **smolagents** | Minimalist, lightweight | Simple agents |

## 🔑 Trends 2026
1. **Graph-based orchestration** (LangGraph) dominates over loop-based
2. **MCP (Model Context Protocol)** — 1000+ servers, standard for tool access
3. **Spec-Driven Development** — GitHub Spec Kit (130k+ stars) makes specs executable
4. **Agent Resource Discovery** — Google's open spec for publishing AI capabilities
5. **Harness engineering** — Evals, memory, permissions, observability as first-class

## 🆕 NEW Trends 2026 (Aug)
1. **Embodied AI systems engineering** — requiring lifecycle governance and human-AI teaming (arXiv:2605.10653) [STUDIED]
2. **Agentic AI for structured, repetitive work** — near-term gains in data-intensive synthesis (arXiv:2604.09633) [NEW]
3. **Local-First Control Planes** — persistent assistants, multi-channel delivery (GitHub: local-ai-coding-guide) [NEW]
4. **AI-generated code outpaces human review** — longitudinal study shows AI writing faster than humans can review (arXiv:2607.01904) [NEW]
5. **Developer well-being in GenAI era** — continuous learning intensifies, need for sustainable practices (arXiv:2605.22349) [NEW]

